Subject: [PATCH 08664/11362] ARC plan 4e: retire before building, premise
 already refuted by existing evidence

Checked the Duck REPL-sandbox bet's premise before building it. Both grounds
it rested on are already dead: (1) the greedy-direct execution model Duck
actually uses is already ported (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5829) and measured 5 times on
gemma-4-31B, all null; (2) the one genuinely novel axis (arbitrary Python vs
a 5-function dispatch table) only matters if multi-step lookahead is the
binding constraint, and the 2026-07-23 lever triangulation found that
bucket empty (0/247 progress actions, two independent runs). Real bottleneck
per that same synthesis: induction-grade sequence routing, "at or near a
genuine capability frontier" -- converges with this session's own
goal-energy zero-gradient finding (4b).

With 4e retired, every item in this plan is now done/negative/redirected/
retired. Documented the two real remaining options (offline goal-progress
signal training, or a fresh SOTA scan first) as strategic decisions for the
operator rather than autonomous next steps.

